[{:db/id 17592186096643 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-32c27023-4101-5727-960c-ccfbce16099a" "question-17cfca30-50dc-5c14-8dd0-380912333363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-32c27023-4101-5727-960c-ccfbce16099a" :question/id #uuid "32c27023-4101-5727-960c-ccfbce16099a" :question/math-academy-id "q-118910" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due west and $|a|=16.$ The vector $b$ is directed vertically up and $|b|=8.$ Find $|a+b|.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a60238ad44009f35ea661e39a2a5c60580f0b56149d0ad372ed52461b348c5.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={16}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\  & =320\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{320}=8\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8fd3f51-46fc-5947-b8e0-a2f5fa5f7025"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8fd3f51-46fc-5947-b8e0-a2f5fa5f7025" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fd3f51-46fc-5947-b8e0-a2f5fa5f7025" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7983f355-aa20-5834-9494-e646a432ba66" "answer-64501922-14f1-5b68-9bb8-4a18b9118b75" "answer-99756e33-2341-5970-963d-037979ab31fc" "answer-45bfd978-6e30-5951-92eb-b82ea3ef3ad2" "answer-27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7983f355-aa20-5834-9494-e646a432ba66" :answer/id #uuid "7983f355-aa20-5834-9494-e646a432ba66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64501922-14f1-5b68-9bb8-4a18b9118b75" :answer/id #uuid "64501922-14f1-5b68-9bb8-4a18b9118b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99756e33-2341-5970-963d-037979ab31fc" :answer/id #uuid "99756e33-2341-5970-963d-037979ab31fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45bfd978-6e30-5951-92eb-b82ea3ef3ad2" :answer/id #uuid "45bfd978-6e30-5951-92eb-b82ea3ef3ad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71" :answer/id #uuid "27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-17cfca30-50dc-5c14-8dd0-380912333363" :question/id #uuid "17cfca30-50dc-5c14-8dd0-380912333363" :question/math-academy-id "q-316807" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due west and $|a|=15.$ The vector $b$ is directed vertically up and $|b|=9.$ Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/a4/a493346a118732d2b435e1757bcbabe756c5d0482aec0688c095b7151352d4c7.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={15}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =306\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{306}=3\\sqrt{34}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0843c3b9-ca94-5b83-889e-fb8a14d6ed3b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0843c3b9-ca94-5b83-889e-fb8a14d6ed3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0843c3b9-ca94-5b83-889e-fb8a14d6ed3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1" :answer/id #uuid "89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-802cdf34-1293-5319-b775-69d99d9605a6" "question-3ba76054-9f72-50d9-a7e8-25a2eccb8d81"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-802cdf34-1293-5319-b775-69d99d9605a6" :question/id #uuid "802cdf34-1293-5319-b775-69d99d9605a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-69501" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d32ceace77d77dc5a3b9b1443b0985232ac23837a5cb5b2b5c6969e7cc65bfef.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a|.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f2/f2144a9accce690363d34c31ed1c29b4742281eb26c273c91a55776c0ad54e5a.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=25\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{25}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,525} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-999d96da-ead9-58f1-95d7-05e3fcaf8038"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-999d96da-ead9-58f1-95d7-05e3fcaf8038" :answer-field/id #uuid "999d96da-ead9-58f1-95d7-05e3fcaf8038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df1422f1-6572-5a6f-9f13-2c4031c88aee" "answer-23af22cb-5a66-56af-8a6e-a750ebfdd947" "answer-3a4098af-5a86-5ee1-b39a-68dcdd7adfb2" "answer-bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" "answer-473e76ef-59a4-58d5-ac39-765fc9788603"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df1422f1-6572-5a6f-9f13-2c4031c88aee" :answer/id #uuid "df1422f1-6572-5a6f-9f13-2c4031c88aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23af22cb-5a66-56af-8a6e-a750ebfdd947" :answer/id #uuid "23af22cb-5a66-56af-8a6e-a750ebfdd947" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a4098af-5a86-5ee1-b39a-68dcdd7adfb2" :answer/id #uuid "3a4098af-5a86-5ee1-b39a-68dcdd7adfb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{15}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" :answer/id #uuid "bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-473e76ef-59a4-58d5-ac39-765fc9788603" :answer/id #uuid "473e76ef-59a4-58d5-ac39-765fc9788603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ba76054-9f72-50d9-a7e8-25a2eccb8d81" :question/id #uuid "3ba76054-9f72-50d9-a7e8-25a2eccb8d81" :question/math-academy-id "q-275711" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a2efe530287edefcee1609c5765d84c9608c5680f80a056819692f80a2e8c0f9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{mm}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition for $a$ and $b.$ We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane. The resultant goes from the start of $a$ to the head of $b.$\n\n![](images/41/41bd69400fe98c2f8ab964c76fa295a6624f83d51fc720ba251ae4c618f87954.png)\n\nNow, in $△AHB,$ we have $m∠AHB={90}^{∘},$ $AH=30\\,\\text{mm},$ and $BH=10\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{900+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1000} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|a+b|=10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79a25629-7a8d-5411-bacd-30c7224e71e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79a25629-7a8d-5411-bacd-30c7224e71e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "79a25629-7a8d-5411-bacd-30c7224e71e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b" :answer/id #uuid "7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096645 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c6713e37-7e62-534f-9e1d-40cff7fc1ed3" "question-4a16473f-5565-58aa-afbf-78ab6b462353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c6713e37-7e62-534f-9e1d-40cff7fc1ed3" :question/id #uuid "c6713e37-7e62-534f-9e1d-40cff7fc1ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11887" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d19c7802a136d6fd039c190acdda94e9e8603d58d2ba62864ea0e5522cbd6791.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=3$ and $|b|=4$, find the value of $|a+b|.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/38/3858242481fec9cd3b3fef85fcbb4e6a17aff20128f47565807a253dba517585.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =9+16+12 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{37}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b243cc54-a33f-576c-b54c-700231d1a2f4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b243cc54-a33f-576c-b54c-700231d1a2f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b243cc54-a33f-576c-b54c-700231d1a2f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12d2a9ec-fb95-5d20-a726-63f5771b10f3" "answer-3f9d5909-94e6-5d98-bed0-36ed77f8c2ef" "answer-390cf7e7-f277-521d-acc2-2719c16d4347" "answer-9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" "answer-845a2766-707b-53f6-be2f-35e563eda9f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12d2a9ec-fb95-5d20-a726-63f5771b10f3" :answer/id #uuid "12d2a9ec-fb95-5d20-a726-63f5771b10f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f9d5909-94e6-5d98-bed0-36ed77f8c2ef" :answer/id #uuid "3f9d5909-94e6-5d98-bed0-36ed77f8c2ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-390cf7e7-f277-521d-acc2-2719c16d4347" :answer/id #uuid "390cf7e7-f277-521d-acc2-2719c16d4347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" :answer/id #uuid "9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-845a2766-707b-53f6-be2f-35e563eda9f7" :answer/id #uuid "845a2766-707b-53f6-be2f-35e563eda9f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a16473f-5565-58aa-afbf-78ab6b462353" :question/id #uuid "4a16473f-5565-58aa-afbf-78ab6b462353" :question/math-academy-id "q-317060" :question/problem "![](images/29/29e3f8ef81b98c4073e934a59f59557d399d105991c2386c3178c3840bd6ac3a.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=5\\sqrt{3}$ and $|b|=6,$ find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/c5/c58fcaace0fd6b1161426357025da18aaccd182b7035db152221bdfddbe28226.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b{|}^{2} & =|a{|}^{2}+|b{|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =(5\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{6}^{2}-2\\cdot (5\\sqrt{3})\\cdot 6\\cdot \\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =75+36+90 \\\\  & =201.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{201}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2c77d03-16e4-5e98-9806-4ae53e282fdb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2c77d03-16e4-5e98-9806-4ae53e282fdb" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c77d03-16e4-5e98-9806-4ae53e282fdb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b" :answer/id #uuid "8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{201}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129214 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b" :question/id #uuid "80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b" :question/math-academy-id "q-99410" :question/problem "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2-5\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=2+5\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-621d2560-2a88-546c-aa01-9273b93c0401"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-621d2560-2a88-546c-aa01-9273b93c0401" :answer-field/id #uuid "621d2560-2a88-546c-aa01-9273b93c0401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-894dd0ee-996e-5946-926e-1667d9661d2f" "answer-27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" "answer-39c17d8b-7383-565d-82ff-9034e842313a" "answer-a5514041-c574-508e-9c48-296d90937fe8" "answer-e0a5c562-7c09-52ed-9124-62137601a6cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-894dd0ee-996e-5946-926e-1667d9661d2f" :answer/id #uuid "894dd0ee-996e-5946-926e-1667d9661d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" :answer/id #uuid "27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39c17d8b-7383-565d-82ff-9034e842313a" :answer/id #uuid "39c17d8b-7383-565d-82ff-9034e842313a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5514041-c574-508e-9c48-296d90937fe8" :answer/id #uuid "a5514041-c574-508e-9c48-296d90937fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0a5c562-7c09-52ed-9124-62137601a6cd" :answer/id #uuid "e0a5c562-7c09-52ed-9124-62137601a6cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129136 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d87763f-3e1e-5f56-b2a4-bc97bccd7687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d87763f-3e1e-5f56-b2a4-bc97bccd7687" :question/id #uuid "8d87763f-3e1e-5f56-b2a4-bc97bccd7687" :question/math-academy-id "q-140502" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above.\nGiven that $A$ has the complex eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2-5\\text{i},$ and that $A=PC{P}^{-1}$ where $C$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, what is the value of \n$\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nSince we are given the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2-5\\text{i},$ we can immediately construct the rotation-scaling matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,{\\lambda }_{1}=-2-5\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2-5\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5+5\\text{i} & 5 \\\\ -10 & 5+5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(-5+5\\text{i}){x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -10{x}_{1}+(5+5\\text{i}){x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\text{i}){x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\text{i}){x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=2$, we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can construct the matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}=\\frac{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-032ad5ea-b156-5e33-a7be-bc141e7f1c34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-032ad5ea-b156-5e33-a7be-bc141e7f1c34" :answer-field/id #uuid "032ad5ea-b156-5e33-a7be-bc141e7f1c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e4b3e5e-e60f-54f8-a180-20a2dffb4c40" :answer-field/choices ["answer-760f31e6-7cca-54b7-8d98-f5aff61070ba" "answer-ee82d2f9-4196-5c21-b0cc-b2a8e520706a" "answer-6e4b3e5e-e60f-54f8-a180-20a2dffb4c40" "answer-dc888f95-a5ef-55ce-b32e-8bfff1554337" "answer-73a0f75c-e27c-550f-b2be-3fd75e2e5ad6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-760f31e6-7cca-54b7-8d98-f5aff61070ba" :answer/id #uuid "760f31e6-7cca-54b7-8d98-f5aff61070ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee82d2f9-4196-5c21-b0cc-b2a8e520706a" :answer/id #uuid "ee82d2f9-4196-5c21-b0cc-b2a8e520706a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e4b3e5e-e60f-54f8-a180-20a2dffb4c40" :answer/id #uuid "6e4b3e5e-e60f-54f8-a180-20a2dffb4c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc888f95-a5ef-55ce-b32e-8bfff1554337" :answer/id #uuid "dc888f95-a5ef-55ce-b32e-8bfff1554337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73a0f75c-e27c-550f-b2be-3fd75e2e5ad6" :answer/id #uuid "73a0f75c-e27c-550f-b2be-3fd75e2e5ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bba7dd75-0519-5756-8558-53f530eff737" :activity/id #uuid "bba7dd75-0519-5756-8558-53f530eff737" :activity/title "Reducing Real 2x2 Matrices to Rotation-Scaling Form" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048584 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-f872b89c-4ebf-575b-acff-0457891853a1" "step-15c2ddcb-4a6a-5d10-92a7-7eac543f5050" "step-ed8df2a4-c822-5ea5-aa21-e1c6c89fb344" "step-7e9b9df9-0488-568f-a29f-8082f11cab44" "step-66c2fbfa-b746-5325-80be-b35737eb36eb"] :activity/first-step "step-f872b89c-4ebf-575b-acff-0457891853a1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f872b89c-4ebf-575b-acff-0457891853a1" :step/id #uuid "f872b89c-4ebf-575b-acff-0457891853a1" :step/content 17592186392266 :step/next "step-15c2ddcb-4a6a-5d10-92a7-7eac543f5050" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-15c2ddcb-4a6a-5d10-92a7-7eac543f5050" :step/id #uuid "15c2ddcb-4a6a-5d10-92a7-7eac543f5050" :step/content 17592186129717 :step/next "step-ed8df2a4-c822-5ea5-aa21-e1c6c89fb344" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ed8df2a4-c822-5ea5-aa21-e1c6c89fb344" :step/id #uuid "ed8df2a4-c822-5ea5-aa21-e1c6c89fb344" :step/content 17592186410857 :step/next "step-7e9b9df9-0488-568f-a29f-8082f11cab44" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7e9b9df9-0488-568f-a29f-8082f11cab44" :step/id #uuid "7e9b9df9-0488-568f-a29f-8082f11cab44" :step/content "question-80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b" :step/next "step-66c2fbfa-b746-5325-80be-b35737eb36eb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-66c2fbfa-b746-5325-80be-b35737eb36eb" :step/id #uuid "66c2fbfa-b746-5325-80be-b35737eb36eb" :step/content "question-8d87763f-3e1e-5f56-b2a4-bc97bccd7687" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119930 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1d6c75b7-d9d1-5c4f-a63e-3df78db605e9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d6c75b7-d9d1-5c4f-a63e-3df78db605e9" :question/id #uuid "1d6c75b7-d9d1-5c4f-a63e-3df78db605e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42946" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $1$st row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(N) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{5})=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(N)=-10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72d0d37d-2da5-57c2-b260-86d1c7a8fa86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72d0d37d-2da5-57c2-b260-86d1c7a8fa86" :answer-field/id #uuid "72d0d37d-2da5-57c2-b260-86d1c7a8fa86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5e28842e-a45a-5471-b0f2-624733f6c02e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5aa48bd6-79d0-527f-843f-9ca1892f691d" "answer-5e28842e-a45a-5471-b0f2-624733f6c02e" "answer-eca12e3d-3b57-505b-bd5b-c92cf39819a7" "answer-593caf3a-5a8a-5474-911c-e4672c977ceb" "answer-0a3d5b37-6c2a-5cba-ad78-e9a2626168b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aa48bd6-79d0-527f-843f-9ca1892f691d" :answer/id #uuid "5aa48bd6-79d0-527f-843f-9ca1892f691d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e28842e-a45a-5471-b0f2-624733f6c02e" :answer/id #uuid "5e28842e-a45a-5471-b0f2-624733f6c02e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db