ep-28439026-9df7-5022-8efd-98cccd4a8a55"] :activity/first-step "step-aacc10c9-f5e2-59c8-9018-6674e86ff34b" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-aacc10c9-f5e2-59c8-9018-6674e86ff34b" :step/id #uuid "aacc10c9-f5e2-59c8-9018-6674e86ff34b" :step/content 17592186097335 :step/next "step-f75a3ecc-4d92-58be-9d26-61d0b71eab9f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f75a3ecc-4d92-58be-9d26-61d0b71eab9f" :step/id #uuid "f75a3ecc-4d92-58be-9d26-61d0b71eab9f" :step/content "question-9756da76-54ed-58bb-84a5-fe67fc16acc7" :step/next "step-28439026-9df7-5022-8efd-98cccd4a8a55" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-28439026-9df7-5022-8efd-98cccd4a8a55" :step/id #uuid "28439026-9df7-5022-8efd-98cccd4a8a55" :step/content "question-e294440f-b12e-5095-aeac-cd3f942d43e6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124588 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-084ad25e-19c6-5ebb-8cd6-5dbb5920b42c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-084ad25e-19c6-5ebb-8cd6-5dbb5920b42c" :question/id #uuid "084ad25e-19c6-5ebb-8cd6-5dbb5920b42c" :question/math-academy-id "q-164413" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $2(y-1)^{2}+4(z+3)^{2}=16$ and the plane $x=3$ onto the $yz$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $x=3,$ we substitute $x=3$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $x$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(y-1)^{2}+4(z+3)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{(2)^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d65f5dbc-0a59-5859-b137-87fda8178c83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d65f5dbc-0a59-5859-b137-87fda8178c83" :answer-field/id #uuid "d65f5dbc-0a59-5859-b137-87fda8178c83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae7ed0f2-f5c6-593b-ac6d-259578441162" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bab2f4b6-64d0-53c0-8f72-8825095fe02e" "answer-9ed0db32-fb84-5446-a9ff-0a2a53498e18" "answer-ae7ed0f2-f5c6-593b-ac6d-259578441162" "answer-aed0ee5c-61e4-5a77-bb58-8b3549ffca96" "answer-acc0a783-47ae-59a6-a47a-b7df839460d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bab2f4b6-64d0-53c0-8f72-8825095fe02e" :answer/id #uuid "bab2f4b6-64d0-53c0-8f72-8825095fe02e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ed0db32-fb84-5446-a9ff-0a2a53498e18" :answer/id #uuid "9ed0db32-fb84-5446-a9ff-0a2a53498e18" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae7ed0f2-f5c6-593b-ac6d-259578441162" :answer/id #uuid "ae7ed0f2-f5c6-593b-ac6d-259578441162" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aed0ee5c-61e4-5a77-bb58-8b3549ffca96" :answer/id #uuid "aed0ee5c-61e4-5a77-bb58-8b3549ffca96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ and $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc0a783-47ae-59a6-a47a-b7df839460d0" :answer/id #uuid "acc0a783-47ae-59a6-a47a-b7df839460d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{2}$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124626 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-126b6d2e-f9ae-5f21-89ee-ad0b88bb4a14"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-126b6d2e-f9ae-5f21-89ee-ad0b88bb4a14" :question/id #uuid "126b6d2e-f9ae-5f21-89ee-ad0b88bb4a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-46965" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x-3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can sketch the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x-3}$ as follows:\n\n1\\. Take the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it to the right by $3$ units. This gives $y=\\frac{1}{x-3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/e3/e3308ad7f61359df7fb4e1b0f32f1d373c703be34b353ffa100ae57c6c115e0b.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x-3}=\\infty ,\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c5abf857-ce1f-5315-be6e-f87c73fa5383"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c5abf857-ce1f-5315-be6e-f87c73fa5383" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5abf857-ce1f-5315-be6e-f87c73fa5383" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7405bf6b-6a0d-5b62-a398-8dece69260f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5fb23454-9977-5191-ad3a-c12baa1c41eb" "answer-4f2985fe-ea8d-5e52-b72c-0a10ddf54913" "answer-be83f313-b20b-5287-9aeb-a58682fcdc0b" "answer-7405bf6b-6a0d-5b62-a398-8dece69260f7" "answer-781f5cee-1530-50ff-9dc8-5cb5770aa8a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fb23454-9977-5191-ad3a-c12baa1c41eb" :answer/id #uuid "5fb23454-9977-5191-ad3a-c12baa1c41eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f2985fe-ea8d-5e52-b72c-0a10ddf54913" :answer/id #uuid "4f2985fe-ea8d-5e52-b72c-0a10ddf54913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be83f313-b20b-5287-9aeb-a58682fcdc0b" :answer/id #uuid "be83f313-b20b-5287-9aeb-a58682fcdc0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7405bf6b-6a0d-5b62-a398-8dece69260f7" :answer/id #uuid "7405bf6b-6a0d-5b62-a398-8dece69260f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-781f5cee-1530-50ff-9dc8-5cb5770aa8a9" :answer/id #uuid "781f5cee-1530-50ff-9dc8-5cb5770aa8a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124575 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b3ded2ac-377c-5a79-a174-a4c453e1b17f" "question-facb659a-1d6a-50ad-a009-4e0f9aa3e331"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b3ded2ac-377c-5a79-a174-a4c453e1b17f" :question/id #uuid "b3ded2ac-377c-5a79-a174-a4c453e1b17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-300982" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{7}{4{(x-2)}^{3}}\\,=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{7}{4{(x-2)}^{3}}=\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{(x-2)}^{3}}\n$$\n\nFor any non-constant polynomial $P(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\pm \\infty }(\\frac{1}{P(x)})=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${(x-2)}^{3}$ is a non-constant polynomial, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the original limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{(x-2)}^{3}}=\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot 0=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d21a9e8-24d8-5f1d-b050-6be0b52be222"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d21a9e8-24d8-5f1d-b050-6be0b52be222" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d21a9e8-24d8-5f1d-b050-6be0b52be222" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-84d61063-c977-5de9-9ee9-751b5700caa9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84d61063-c977-5de9-9ee9-751b5700caa9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84d61063-c977-5de9-9ee9-751b5700caa9" :answer/id #uuid "84d61063-c977-5de9-9ee9-751b5700caa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-facb659a-1d6a-50ad-a009-4e0f9aa3e331" :question/id #uuid "facb659a-1d6a-50ad-a009-4e0f9aa3e331" :question/math-academy-id "q-334183" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-12}{9{(x+5)}^{4}}\\,=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-12}{9{(x+5)}^{4}}=\\frac{-12}{9}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{(x+5)}^{4}}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{(x+5)}^{4}}\n$$\n\nFor any non-constant polynomial $P(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\pm \\infty }(\\frac{1}{P(x)})=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${(x+5)}^{4}$ is a non-constant polynomial, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{(x+5)^{4}}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the original limit as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{(x+5)}^{4}}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 0=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d76b44d-6cd7-5750-b38b-774c366dedf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d76b44d-6cd7-5750-b38b-774c366dedf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d76b44d-6cd7-5750-b38b-774c366dedf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fd970ca4-531c-5efa-b2d5-8a2654d8cfb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd970ca4-531c-5efa-b2d5-8a2654d8cfb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd970ca4-531c-5efa-b2d5-8a2654d8cfb9" :answer/id #uuid "fd970ca4-531c-5efa-b2d5-8a2654d8cfb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a655a425-a6ac-5f15-b67b-b68bfc4e40c2" :activity/id #uuid "a655a425-a6ac-5f15-b67b-b68bfc4e40c2" :activity/title "Limits of Reciprocal Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048515 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-5f34953f-75de-56f9-a16f-93dfa8832257" "step-1086f6d0-8fdf-5383-ace5-80814d556034" "step-6127401a-4b3b-5612-a426-5ddbe9b9c8f9"] :activity/first-step "step-5f34953f-75de-56f9-a16f-93dfa8832257" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5f34953f-75de-56f9-a16f-93dfa8832257" :step/id #uuid "5f34953f-75de-56f9-a16f-93dfa8832257" :step/content "question-126b6d2e-f9ae-5f21-89ee-ad0b88bb4a14" :step/next "step-1086f6d0-8fdf-5383-ace5-80814d556034" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1086f6d0-8fdf-5383-ace5-80814d556034" :step/id #uuid "1086f6d0-8fdf-5383-ace5-80814d556034" :step/content "question-b3ded2ac-377c-5a79-a174-a4c453e1b17f" :step/next "step-6127401a-4b3b-5612-a426-5ddbe9b9c8f9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6127401a-4b3b-5612-a426-5ddbe9b9c8f9" :step/id #uuid "6127401a-4b3b-5612-a426-5ddbe9b9c8f9" :step/content "question-facb659a-1d6a-50ad-a009-4e0f9aa3e331" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-87ece511-fd94-56a1-8fa2-055336c9156b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-87ece511-fd94-56a1-8fa2-055336c9156b" :question/id #uuid "87ece511-fd94-56a1-8fa2-055336c9156b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48848" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}$ at the point where $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3{x}^{2}+24.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 6x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting  $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-2} & ={(\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}})|}_{x=-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{\\sqrt{3(-2)^{2}+24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5afb038d-0b31-5d55-8f54-c760388f6c4b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5afb038d-0b31-5d55-8f54-c760388f6c4b" :answer-field/id #uuid "5afb038d-0b31-5d55-8f54-c760388f6c4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2440da94-c49c-5b97-93a3-f1f305aaf546" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2440da94-c49c-5b97-93a3-f1f305aaf546" "answer-fd4a6f37-6e13-59de-b1f0-4ae8dde2510a" "answer-4dfdfa0c-df5d-578c-9e5a-030e1e19fe81" "answer-67441758-f1aa-545c-a9ad-7fa7f49bf8b9" "answer-fb5ed5a3-55f9-5465-8515-fdd310345cd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2440da94-c49c-5b97-93a3-f1f305aaf546" :answer/id #uuid "2440da94-c49c-5b97-93a3-f1f305aaf546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd4a6f37-6e13-59de-b1f0-4ae8dde2510a" :answer/id #uuid "fd4a6f37-6e13-59de-b1f0-4ae8dde2510a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dfdfa0c-df5d-578c-9e5a-030e1e19fe81" :answer/id #uuid "4dfdfa0c-df5d-578c-9e5a-030e1e19fe81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67441758-f1aa-545c-a9ad-7fa7f49bf8b9" :answer/id #uuid "67441758-f1aa-545c-a9ad-7fa7f49bf8b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb5ed5a3-55f9-5465-8515-fdd310345cd7" :answer/id #uuid "fb5ed5a3-55f9-5465-8515-fdd310345cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d6e7296-3732-5370-89a1-2dbb983a355c" "question-e5c85892-5c29-5ec5-80d2-d47ed89d83b9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d6e7296-3732-5370-89a1-2dbb983a355c" :question/id #uuid "9d6e7296-3732-5370-89a1-2dbb983a355c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71951" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})^{′}=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bbfbd138-787c-5944-9a48-89b79ecd75b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bbfbd138-787c-5944-9a48-89b79ecd75b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbfbd138-787c-5944-9a48-89b79ecd75b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-baf7a497-5f73-5773-889e-5e6f697822ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82e6a967-6c7d-5d88-8afe-9d6fff949b45" "answer-baf7a497-5f73-5773-889e-5e6f697822ac" "answer-df3cad62-492d-5cb0-b710-42db57802071" "answer-caaa2a22-48c5-53fe-92ea-da472c888e6f" "answer-557cd32f-67a1-5f7d-8007-8e8dc4e07e92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e6a967-6c7d-5d88-8afe-9d6fff949b45" :answer/id #uuid "82e6a967-6c7d-5d88-8afe-9d6fff949b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baf7a497-5f73-5773-889e-5e6f697822ac" :answer/id #uuid "baf7a497-5f73-5773-889e-5e6f697822ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df3cad62-492d-5cb0-b710-42db57802071" :answer/id #uuid "df3cad62-492d-5cb0-b710-42db57802071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}){(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caaa2a22-48c5-53fe-92ea-da472c888e6f" :answer/id #uuid "caaa2a22-48c5-53fe-92ea-da472c888e6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-3{x}^{2})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-557cd32f-67a1-5f7d-8007-8e8dc4e07e92" :answer/id #uuid "557cd32f-67a1-5f7d-8007-8e8dc4e07e92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})}^{2}(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e5c85892-5c29-5ec5-80d2-d47ed89d83b9" :question/id #uuid "e5c85892-5c29-5ec5-80d2-d47ed89d83b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-107298" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x-{x}^{2}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=x-{x}^{2}$ and $f(g(x))=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{g}}=-4{g}^{-1/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =-4({g}^{-1/2})^{′}=4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{g}^{-3/2}=\\frac{2}{{g}^{3/2}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(x-{x}^{2})^{′}=1-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{g}^{3/2}}\\cdot (1-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2-4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c878ff99-495e-5613-8683-22e308482f13"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c878ff99-495e-5613-8683-22e308482f13" :answer-field/id #uuid "c878ff99-495e-5613-8683-22e308482f13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f88f7c0f-9d24-5617-aa25-c79abffb93e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c895d3ba-c44d-57f2-8b2f-97e98d154d5d" "answer-de570552-69e0-5331-86f3-79143ee949ab" "answer-528cbd11-0bdd-5861-899e-cfe78186526c" "answer-096b9b79-42b4-5435-8d17-15938cf8083f" "answer-f88f7c0f-9d24-5617-aa25-c79abffb93e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c895d3ba-c44d-57f2-8b2f-97e98d154d5d" :answer/id #uuid "c895d3ba-c44d-57f2-8b2f-97e98d154d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1-2x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de570552-69e0-5331-86f3-79143ee949ab" :answer/id #uuid "de570552-69e0-5331-86f3-79143ee949ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2+4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-528cbd11-0bdd-5861-899e-cfe78186526c" :answer/id #uuid "528cbd11-0bdd-5861-899e-cfe78186526c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-2x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-096b9b79-42b4-5435-8d17-15938cf8083f" :answer/id #uuid "096b9b79-42b4-5435-8d17-15938cf8083f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+4x}{\\sqrt{x-{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f88f7c0f-9d24-5617-aa25-c79abffb93e6" :answer/id #uuid "f88f7c0f-9d24-5617-aa25-c79abffb93e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ab618439-d4b6-5529-9e3d-c044191c43d2" :activity/id #uuid "ab618439-d4b6-5529-9e3d-c044191c43d2" :activity/title "The Chain Rule for Differentiation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051084 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-3e13e019-bb52-5d8f-95f9-937af8f29b8f" "step-439bf3c9-9c86-5ea1-bcba-ed795ff54c05" "step-3f12b7e4-e0e1-5d0d-aa45-c42523632b41"] :activity/first-step "step-3e13e019-bb52-5d8f-95f9-937af8f29b8f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3e13e019-bb52-5d8f-95f9-937af8f29b8f" :step/id #uuid "3e13e019-bb52-5d8f-95f9-937af8f29b8f" :step/content "question-87ece511-fd94-56a1-8fa2-055336c9156b" :step/next "step-439bf3c9-9c86-5ea1-bcba-ed795ff54c05" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-439bf3c9-9c86-5ea1-bcba-ed795ff54c05" :step/id #uuid "439bf3c9-9c86-5ea1-bcba-ed795ff54c05" :step/content "question-9d6e7296-3732-5370-89a1-2dbb983a355c" :step/next "step-3f12b7e4-e0e1-5d0d-aa45-c42523632b41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3f12b7e4-e0e1-5d0d-aa45-c42523632b41" :step/id #uuid "3f12b7e4-e0e1-5d0d-aa45-c42523632b41" :step/content "question-e5c85892-5c29-5ec5-80d2-d47ed89d83b9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4b0fcd8a-2ef6-570d-b9d5-23a0ce190bc1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b0fcd8a-2ef6-570d-b9d5-23a0ce190bc1" :question/id #uuid "4b0fcd8a-2ef6-570d-b9d5-23a0ce190bc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182389" :question/problem "If $A$ is false, then $A⇒B$ is\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is false, then $A⇒B$ is $\\text{always true}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $F$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dfd11c04-f5c0-5a2a-967d-efee14d871ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dfd11c04-f5c0-5a2a-967d-efee14d871ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfd11c04-f5c0-5a2a-967d-efee14d871ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fa3bcf1d-d459-521d-b1c3-9f9fbce7b8b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97b80483-fe65-55cb-9038-8211ba61f54c" "answer-fa3bcf1d-d459-521d-b1c3-9f9fbce7b8b1" "answer-ab8c2dd6-4a11-53bd-aa21-fab81d9eba5e" "answ