l to $\\overset{\\to }{UV}?$" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{UV},$ we divide $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{UV}}{|\\overset{\\to }{UV}|}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=3\\overset{\\to }{UV}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-537d3cf5-0d6e-5a1b-96fe-52ba35118a33"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-537d3cf5-0d6e-5a1b-96fe-52ba35118a33" :answer-field/id #uuid "537d3cf5-0d6e-5a1b-96fe-52ba35118a33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-052d695c-75c2-537a-b2dd-d40fb706a504" "answer-31d03316-8870-51ff-8acc-393b2704b5f7" "answer-77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" "answer-4d4e311b-d223-5cb9-82e6-b49ae0b379b8" "answer-2b72b380-5234-5f6a-925b-f6a08d294796"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-052d695c-75c2-537a-b2dd-d40fb706a504" :answer/id #uuid "052d695c-75c2-537a-b2dd-d40fb706a504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31d03316-8870-51ff-8acc-393b2704b5f7" :answer/id #uuid "31d03316-8870-51ff-8acc-393b2704b5f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" :answer/id #uuid "77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d4e311b-d223-5cb9-82e6-b49ae0b379b8" :answer/id #uuid "4d4e311b-d223-5cb9-82e6-b49ae0b379b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b72b380-5234-5f6a-925b-f6a08d294796" :answer/id #uuid "2b72b380-5234-5f6a-925b-f6a08d294796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf062e19-facf-5f56-9031-7ed68b8d30bc" "question-cb1f02a3-6465-553f-a943-f356abc8fd01"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf062e19-facf-5f56-9031-7ed68b8d30bc" :question/id #uuid "bf062e19-facf-5f56-9031-7ed68b8d30bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275627" :question/problem "![](images/13/13fc8ff564a7162c556d050a10df6e8f23c0fca269e3b88168ca6681be3ad3a3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $p+q$ and has the same direction as $p+q.$ \n\nType $p$ and $q$ to represent the vectors $p$ and $q,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $p+q.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $p+q$ goes from the tail of $p$ to the head of $q:$ \n\n![](images/68/68c14ce5ff66272986e958f09f30289d56519e90b34fae23362753f84c042a50.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=3.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|p+q| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p+q$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|p+q|}\\cdot (p+q) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a9adad1-9941-5e52-a6d0-5821492aa5a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a9adad1-9941-5e52-a6d0-5821492aa5a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9adad1-9941-5e52-a6d0-5821492aa5a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926" :answer/id #uuid "d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097161 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb1f02a3-6465-553f-a943-f356abc8fd01" :question/id #uuid "cb1f02a3-6465-553f-a943-f356abc8fd01" :question/math-academy-id "q-119796" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa72f6ea8c52a1f141f8469c3f932937b8b957956dc478811910e77c83336a9c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $p?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/4d/4d4d7faa0c0611c8ef891cda5fef3b75a61aa97e0879fac525f58f4ce263c937.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=5.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p$ is $\\sqrt{29}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|\\,p\\,|}\\cdot p \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3de6837-e66c-5b9a-a142-8fdce8446005"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3de6837-e66c-5b9a-a142-8fdce8446005" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3de6837-e66c-5b9a-a142-8fdce8446005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b80ef2f2-4a9b-5e69-872c-2881d1a0e191" "answer-c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" "answer-133b9a0b-07a3-5279-9f37-33049aaaa2e0" "answer-f784eacd-53c7-568d-957e-7b132d8f2939" "answer-b626256e-983a-5f2c-9230-3938cb23814d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b80ef2f2-4a9b-5e69-872c-2881d1a0e191" :answer/id #uuid "b80ef2f2-4a9b-5e69-872c-2881d1a0e191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{29}p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" :answer/id #uuid "c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-133b9a0b-07a3-5279-9f37-33049aaaa2e0" :answer/id #uuid "133b9a0b-07a3-5279-9f37-33049aaaa2e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}}p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f784eacd-53c7-568d-957e-7b132d8f2939" :answer/id #uuid "f784eacd-53c7-568d-957e-7b132d8f2939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b626256e-983a-5f2c-9230-3938cb23814d" :answer/id #uuid "b626256e-983a-5f2c-9230-3938cb23814d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-64f8dbbc-bd8d-5e6e-b9e2-32a2e83cd44b" "question-2f3e6ef6-a3b7-556b-876b-54d269e801f3" "question-46e2433f-faec-5a20-b0d6-cabb5029813a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-64f8dbbc-bd8d-5e6e-b9e2-32a2e83cd44b" :question/id #uuid "64f8dbbc-bd8d-5e6e-b9e2-32a2e83cd44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-77229" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $|\\,a\\,|=7$, while the vector $b$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,b\\,|=7.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/94/9468530a650f0bee117a4254aa87b5954c7bbbe2684d95f9db3f9961026abcb2.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={7}^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{98}=7\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ecbe05ce-5c99-5a55-b52c-2b92b42e1761"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecbe05ce-5c99-5a55-b52c-2b92b42e1761" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecbe05ce-5c99-5a55-b52c-2b92b42e1761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25d977df-2058-5b96-8d7e-8459946ef00d" "answer-c628653b-f32f-521c-a5ac-5e6e7ac0095c" "answer-926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" "answer-c76d32fd-0d07-5a6f-a42b-f98aee2a62ec" "answer-4b4ca2cc-f364-53e7-b5d7-754b69c071d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d977df-2058-5b96-8d7e-8459946ef00d" :answer/id #uuid "25d977df-2058-5b96-8d7e-8459946ef00d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c628653b-f32f-521c-a5ac-5e6e7ac0095c" :answer/id #uuid "c628653b-f32f-521c-a5ac-5e6e7ac0095c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{6}}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" :answer/id #uuid "926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c76d32fd-0d07-5a6f-a42b-f98aee2a62ec" :answer/id #uuid "c76d32fd-0d07-5a6f-a42b-f98aee2a62ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b4ca2cc-f364-53e7-b5d7-754b69c071d6" :answer/id #uuid "4b4ca2cc-f364-53e7-b5d7-754b69c071d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{98}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f3e6ef6-a3b7-556b-876b-54d269e801f3" :question/id #uuid "2f3e6ef6-a3b7-556b-876b-54d269e801f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-77227" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,a\\,|=5$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-west and $|\\,b\\,|=12.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/15/153aff405a3ae0859ff74fcb98deb09e038db7b033cbe54223866c9fe1724fb1.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}+{12}^{2} \\\\  & =169\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{169}=13,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85ffb2ee-f378-58a7-b51e-ef917e3a8dac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85ffb2ee-f378-58a7-b51e-ef917e3a8dac" :answer-field/id #uuid "85ffb2ee-f378-58a7-b51e-ef917e3a8dac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" "answer-d5e39e22-a209-599e-8108-7f028d51f9b2" "answer-c168b279-f15c-5669-a575-1c75c357532e" "answer-d726cf39-50e8-5e85-a32e-868dc97d0467" "answer-39a84a6a-bccf-512e-adc7-a3b19071646f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" :answer/id #uuid "0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e39e22-a209-599e-8108-7f028d51f9b2" :answer/id #uuid "d5e39e22-a209-599e-8108-7f028d51f9b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c168b279-f15c-5669-a575-1c75c357532e" :answer/id #uuid "c168b279-f15c-5669-a575-1c75c357532e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d726cf39-50e8-5e85-a32e-868dc97d0467" :answer/id #uuid "d726cf39-50e8-5e85-a32e-868dc97d0467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{173}}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39a84a6a-bccf-512e-adc7-a3b19071646f" :answer/id #uuid "39a84a6a-bccf-512e-adc7-a3b19071646f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}(a+b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46e2433f-faec-5a20-b0d6-cabb5029813a" :question/id #uuid "46e2433f-faec-5a20-b0d6-cabb5029813a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275632" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $\\sqrt{3}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $\\sqrt{6}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$ \n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$ \n\n![](images/b7/b7d45d7cd1ea2c61961da8279d3f8702d3e52092fc6aab75a94d3b5076928dba.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{9}=3,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0b511d2-5952-5b68-a426-4cf5aaba9091"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0b511d2-5952-5b68-a426-4cf5aaba9091" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b511d2-5952-5b68-a426-4cf5aaba9091" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787" :answer/id #uuid "0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097833 :tutorial/content "A **unit vector** is a vector whose magnitude is equal to $1.$ \n\nGiven any vector $\\mathbf a$, we can create a unit vector $\\mathbf u$ by dividing $\\mathbf a$ by its magnitude $|\\, \\mathbf{a} \\,|,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{a} }{ |\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,| }\n$$\n\nFor example, if $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=2,$ then the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.\n$$\n\n![](images/c7/c78d5b75c1d5928e7b269a4a67229487b3d3324e9815b11c5fd1f47f63437d82.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096884 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157272 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-313d3071-09f6-580e-b25a-e255d0b523db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-313d3071-09f6-580e-b25a-e255d0b523db" :question/id #uuid "313d3071-09f6-580e-b25a-e255d0b523db" :question/math-academy-id "q-81596" :question/problem "Which statement is equivalent to $(A∨B)∧C?$" :question/worked-solution "We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:\n\n$$\n(A∨B)∧C≡(A∧C)∨(B∧C)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8907b826-36c7-56f1-bb87-457daede6136"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8907b826-36c7-56f1-bb87-457daede6136" :answer-field/id #uuid "8907b826-36c7-56f1-bb87-457daede6136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-04a9d566-a1d7-589e-b4f9-96d5fc2ba6eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00e5fac4-92b9-5315-8d7e-12697e2cb357" "answer-76f4994e-9b50-5371-a554-609109e63cfc" "answer-04a9d566-a1d7-589e-b4f9-96d5fc2ba6eb" "answer-984dba87-8845-55bd-9353-66c604f17e74" "answer-bbf16072-ce91-5690-a8f8-5f5dfab4de0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00e5fac4-92b9-5315-8d7e-12697e2cb357" :answer/id #uuid "00e5fac4-92b9-5315-8d7e-12697e2cb357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(A∧B)∨C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76f4994e-9b50-5371-a554-609109e63cfc" :answer/id #uuid "76f4994e-9b50-5371-a554-609109e63cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(A∧C)∧(B∧C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04a9d566-a1d7-589e-b4f9-96d5fc2ba6eb" :answer/id #uuid "04a9d566-a1d7-589e-b4f9-96d5fc2ba6eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(A∧C)∨(B∧C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-984dba87-8845-55bd-9353-66c604f17e74" :answer/id #uuid "984dba87-8845-55bd-9353-66c604f17e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(A∨C)∨(B∨C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbf16072-ce91-5690-a8f8-5f5dfab4de0b" :answer/id #uuid "bbf16072-ce91-5690-a8f8-5f5d