e for the part in the inner-most parentheses, $A∧B.$ The statement $A∧B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nNext, we look at the columns labeled $A$ and $A∧B$ to complete a truth table for the part in the parentheses, $(A∧B)∨A.$ The statement $(A∧B)∨A$ is true if either $A∧B$ is true, $A$ is true, or both $A∧B$ and $A$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nFinally, we look at the columns labeled $B$ and $(A∧B)∨A$ to complete the column $((A∧B)∨A)∧B.$ The statement $((A∧B)∨A)∧B$ is true if both $(A∧B)∨A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨A\\,$ | $\\,((A∧B)∨A)∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2bd44a91-6ee8-53af-bbcb-a136a444c2c5" "answer-field-ff31c793-d272-5b5a-84c4-702d95e9a393" "answer-field-d0e75173-70c9-5656-a29a-5f55c5429a62" "answer-field-c830e066-bb1f-5a29-bc35-13f551ddd4b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bd44a91-6ee8-53af-bbcb-a136a444c2c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd44a91-6ee8-53af-bbcb-a136a444c2c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :a